  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Government of Kenya in the Implementation of API/PNR Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to the Government of Kenya&#x2019;s endeavour to enhance passenger processing and strengthen traveller identification management capacities and API/PNR establishment and implementation. The project will provide comprehensive support to the Government of Kenya on implementation of API/PNR systems in Kenya, and will complement activities of the United Nations Countering Terrorist Travel Programme (CTTP), through the following activity areas: Inter-departmental consultations; Awareness-raising of national authorities; Operationalization of Passenger Information Unit and capacity-building of end-users; Improved coordination between Points of Entry/Exit (PoEs); Enhanced inter-operability; and setting up a Regional informal working group. The regional IWG will provide a forum for Passenger Information Units (PIUs) as well as for the policy makers involved in the establishment of such units in East Africa to support the implementation of UN Security Council resolutions 2178 (2014), 2396 (2017), and 2482 (2019).</narrative>
  </description>
